course: dictionary
lesson: 11178
title: Winter, the season and the verb
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Winter is the coldest season of the year, and it comes between autumn and spring. Context clues often tell you what a word means. «The Earth's axis is tilted, so away from the equator summer days are long and winter days are short.» Short days in a cold season show that winter is a time of year.
explain: Winter can also be a verb, but it is rare. It means to spend the winter somewhere. «Birds winter in the south» means birds spend the cold months in a warmer place. To check, swap your meaning into the sentence: «Birds spend the winter in the south» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Other clues help too. «A hedgehog curled up in a pile of leaves in winter may breathe only a few times a minute.» The winter cold is the reason its body slows right down. Winter is also part of phrases you may meet, such as winter coat, winter sports, mid-winter and wintry.
fact: Winter is the coldest season of the year, between autumn (fall) and spring.
fact: Winter happens because the Earth is tilted, so your half of the Earth leans away from the Sun and the days are short and cold.
fact: In the Northern Hemisphere, such as the USA, UK, Canada and Ireland, winter is December to February.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, winter is June to August, because their seasons are the other way round.
fact: As a verb, «winter» means to spend the winter somewhere, as in «Birds winter in the south».
exercise: What is winter? | *The coldest season of the year, between autumn and spring | A warm coat you wear outside | The hottest season of the year | The wet season after the summer rains
exercise: «Birds winter in the south.» What does winter mean in this sentence? | Sing loudly | *Spend the winter somewhere | Fly very high | Build a nest in a tree
exercise: In which months is winter in the UK? | *December to February | June to August | September to November | March to May
test: «A hedgehog curled up in a pile of leaves in winter may breathe only a few times a minute.» Why does the hedgehog breathe so slowly? | It is angry | It is running away from a fox | *Its whole body has slowed down to save energy | It has a bad cold
test: In which months is winter in Australia? | *June to August | December to February | March to May | September to November
exam: «A boy in Alaska walking home in winter darkness with a reflective band can be seen from far away.» Why does the reflective band help? | It stops the rain getting into his eyes | It makes him look taller | It keeps him warm in the cold | *It shines the headlights straight back to the driver
